Here's your deploy workflow, tailored to how this repo actually works:

---

## Quick Text Change → Production

**This is a static HTML site** (not Next.js). Pages live in `/public/*.html`. No framework build needed.

### 1. Find and edit the file
```bash
grep -r "old text" /Users/winfredquek/crestbrick-consult/public/ -l
```
Then read the file and make your edit directly.

### 2. Nav changed? Run the stamp script
```bash
cd /Users/winfredquek/crestbrick-consult && npm run build
```
Body-text-only change? Skip this step entirely.

### 3. Review the diff
```bash
git -C /Users/winfredquek/crestbrick-consult diff
```

### 4. Commit and push to `main`
```bash
git -C /Users/winfredquek/crestbrick-consult add public/your-file.html
git -C /Users/winfredquek/crestbrick-consult commit -m "fix: [describe the change]"
git -C /Users/winfredquek/crestbrick-consult push origin main
```
Push to `main` = auto-deploy to production. Vercel picks it up immediately.

### 5. Verify live (~60 seconds)
```bash
curl -s https://winfredquek.com/your-page | grep "your new text"
```
Or open the page in an incognito window to bypass browser cache.

